# Isolated/symlinked install layout (pnpm-style) instead of the flat hoisted
# one: one physical copy per package version under `node_modules/.store/` plus
# symlinks, which deduplicates the react-aria ecosystem and shrinks the tree.
#
# Two consequences worth knowing:
# - `cap sync` resolves the Capacitor plugins through the symlinks and bakes the
#   real `../node_modules/.store/<pkg>@<ver>-<hash>/...` paths into the committed
#   native project files. That hash is derived from the plugin's dependency
#   sub-graph in the lockfile — not from the machine — so the paths are valid
#   everywhere the lockfile is identical, and only move when a plugin's
#   dependency bumps (rerun `make mobile-build`, which is required after a fresh
#   checkout anyway).
# - The tree must stay visible on the host (no named Docker volume over
#   `node_modules`): Gradle and Xcode read the plugins from it. See compose.yaml.
install-strategy=linked

# Supply-chain cooldown: only resolve package versions that have been public for
# at least this many DAYS (npm >= 11.16). Blunts "publish malware, get pulled in
# instantly" attacks by refusing brand-new releases when the tree is (re)resolved
# at `npm install` time. Frozen `npm ci` installs the already-vetted lockfile as
# is. Complements the check:deps guardrail (scripts/check-node-modules.mjs).
min-release-age=1
